Package 174's README: "套包時那支測試以包裡的為準". Its [19] was off here since the 10-08 merge because it tests the laptop's ST02-P2
(package 155 WebMainScanKey.cpp: a soft key sets golden's own bAse* flag, so ScanPannelKey treats it as a physical press -- a soft ALARM
RESET also silences the music / N07 buzzer as golden, a soft RESET honours bDisibleResetButton), while the machine still ran cpp 0153's
key-id hook (returned before the key blocks, skipping those side effects). Now: WebMainScanKey.cpp = package 155's ST02-P2 version +
the machine-local W906_SoftEmergencyStop at the end (RULINGS_20261005 #17; unread soft keys are dropped by clearing the bAse* flags,
fHome read through W906_FormShowing); tests/test_scankey_golden.cpp = the package's file ([19] on); tests/test_main_scankey.cpp [13]
checks the bAse* flags. ckernel.cpp's W906_VirtualPanelKeyHook is no longer set (stays null). WORKLOG row 214.
Debug wb_serve + ScanKeyGolden / MainScanKey / FShow_Audit (on the known-failure list until now) + 3 more pass; release wb_serve built.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
